cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CytoBridge in your research, please cite the following paper."
title: "Beyond per-pair correlation: a drug-discrimination control exposes prediction collapse in single-cell multi-drug perturbation models"
authors:
  - given-names: Xichen
    family-names: Zhao
  - given-names: Guanxing
    family-names: Chen
year: 2025
journal: "Preprint submitted to Elsevier"
repository-code: "https://github.com/schambergeredmund7111992-cmyk/cytobridge-benchmark"
abstract: "CytoBridge fuses frozen scGPT cell embeddings and MolFormer-XL drug embeddings through a pathway-gated cross-attention bridge, followed by a ZINB decoder for single-cell logFC prediction. This repository is a diagnostic study that exposes prediction collapse in single-cell perturbation models through an off-diagonal drug-discrimination control."
keywords:
  - single-cell perturbation
  - drug response prediction
  - foundation model
  - cross-modal fusion
  - pathway gating
  - prediction collapse
  - drug-discrimination control
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21911960
license: MIT
